            <ArticleTitle>A microRNA-activated molecular machine for non-enzymatic target recycling amplification detection of microRNA from cancer cells.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>11084-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c5cc03723a</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The presence of the microRNA-141 target molecules activates the DNA molecular machine powered by the DNA fuel strands, leading to non-enzymatic target cyclic reuse of microRNA-141 and significantly amplified fluorescent signals for sensitive monitoring of microRNA-141 from low numbers of human prostate cancer cells.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
